WEBVTT

1
00:01:18.041 --> 00:01:20.416
In the previous verses, Lord Krishna

2
00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:24.083
began describing His various vibhutis.

3
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:27.875
Now in these four verses, He reveals

4
00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:29.458
His divine manifestations

5
00:01:29.458 --> 00:01:31.041
even more deeply.

6
00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:33.875
These descriptions give devotees a way

7
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:35.541
to understand Lord Krishna's

8
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:39.541
glory through the extraordinary
elements of the world.

9
00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:46.166
In verse 10.25,

10
00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:48.083
Lord Krishna identifies Himself

11
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:50.583
as Bhrigu among the maharishis.

12
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:52.916
Bhrigu was born of Brahma.

13
00:01:52.916 --> 00:01:54.500
He is a great example

14
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.291
of spiritual power and knowledge.

15
00:01:57.291 --> 00:02:01.541
Among sounds, He is the
supreme syllable Omkar.

16
00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:04.166
This sound is the symbol of the supreme truth.

17
00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:06.833
It is also the very essence of the Vedas.

18
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:10.166
Among yajnas, Lord Krishna is japa.

19
00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:13.208
Japa means the loving chanting

20
00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:16.625
and remembrance of the Lord's sacred names.

21
00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:17.541
In this japa-yajna,

22
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:20.583
the direct participation

23
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.250
of our consciousness is needed.

24
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.000
When we chant with attention,

25
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.833
it becomes a personal, devotional service

26
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:31.291
offered to the Lord.

27
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:34.791
Among immovable things,
Lord Krishna is the Himalayas.

28
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:37.791
It is awe-inspiring and unshakeable.

29
00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:39.208
It is a symbol of His eternal

30
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:42.458
and unmoving nature.

31
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:44.500
This verse shows the journey

32
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.541
from outer ritual to inner devotion.

33
00:02:47.541 --> 00:02:48.750
Chanting Lord Krishna's

34
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.583
names engages the mind in His
remembrance, purifies it,

35
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:56.833
and turns it toward divine love.

36
00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:58.375
In verse 10.26,

37
00:02:58.375 --> 00:02:59.625
Lord Krishna gives examples

38
00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:02.375
from nature and divine beings.

39
00:03:02.375 --> 00:03:03.750
He says that among trees,

40
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.166
He is the Ashvattha – the banyan tree.

41
00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:09.583
This tree is long-lived

42
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:12.375
and extremely strong.

43
00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:15.958
Among the divine rishis, Lord Krishna is Narada.

44
00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:18.208
Narada is renowned for devotion.

45
00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:20.000
Throughout the entire universe,

46
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.583
he spreads Lord Krishna's devotion.

47
00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:25.208
Narada is an ideal devotee

48
00:03:25.208 --> 00:03:28.291
who through story, kirtan, and knowledge,

49
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:32.416
strives to connect all of creation to the Lord.

50
00:03:32.416 --> 00:03:34.791
He says further that among the Gandharvas,

51
00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:38.500
He is Chitraratha, the most skilled musician,

52
00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.666
a symbol of beauty and art.

53
00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:44.750
Among the Siddhas, Lord Krishna is Kapila Muni.

54
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.541
He gave the profound

55
00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:49.666
teachings of Sankhya philosophy,
through which

56
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:53.000
humanity can advance on
the path of liberation.

57
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.041
In verse 10.27, Lord Krishna identifies Himself

58
00:03:56.041 --> 00:03:59.125
with divine animals and human rulers.

59
00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:00.541
He says that among horses,

60
00:04:00.541 --> 00:04:02.875
He is Uchchaihshravas.

61
00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:06.083
This is a divine horse born
from the churning of the ocean,

62
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:10.583
a symbol of beauty, speed, and glory.

63
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.583
Among elephants, Lord Krishna is Airavata.

64
00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:15.625
This is Indra's divine elephant.

65
00:04:15.625 --> 00:04:19.000
It is a symbol of strength and majesty.

66
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.125
Among human beings, Lord Krishna is the king.

67
00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:23.458
The king represents leadership

68
00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:26.250
and justice.

69
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.625
According to the Vedic texts, the king's role

70
00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:31.333
is to protect dharma

71
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:34.333
and care for the people.

72
00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:37.000
In verse 10.28, Lord Krishna says

73
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.750
that among weapons, He is the Vajra.

74
00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.875
This is Indra's divine weapon,

75
00:04:41.875 --> 00:04:45.291
a symbol of unmatched power.

76
00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:47.875
Among cows, Lord Krishna is Kamadhenu,

77
00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:51.000
the wish-fulfilling cow.

78
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.125
It is a symbol of Lord Krishna's infinite grace.

79
00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:57.000
Among the causes of progeny,

80
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.416
Lord Krishna is Kandarpa – Kamadeva.

81
00:05:00.416 --> 00:05:05.208
Begetting children for the growth of the family –

82
00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:07.166
but only in the context

83
00:05:07.166 --> 00:05:09.125
of righteous union.

84
00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:10.916
Lord Krishna distinguishes between lust

85
00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:15.041
and pure, sacred attraction.

86
00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:17.541
Among serpents, He is Vasuki.

87
00:05:17.541 --> 00:05:19.916
In the churning of the ocean, Vasuki

88
00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:23.250
was used as the churning rope.

89
00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.166
By meditating on these vibhutis with devotion

90
00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:29.458
and knowing Lord Krishna's all-
pervading presence,

91
00:05:29.458 --> 00:05:34.791
we deepen our relationship with Him.

92
00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:37.208
In the coming verses, Lord Krishna

93
00:05:37.208 --> 00:05:40.625
will describe even more of His vibhutis.

94
00:05:45.166 --> 00:05:47.750
Among all yajnas,

95
00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.250
I am

96
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.958
japa –

97
00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:55.791
the chanting

98
00:05:55.791 --> 00:05:58.583
of sacred names and mantras.

99
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:01.083
This is a simple

100
00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:03.916
yet profound practice.

101
00:06:03.916 --> 00:06:07.375
A way to connect with Me

102
00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:10.791
that you can do at home, at work,

103
00:06:10.791 --> 00:06:13.583
or wherever you are,

104
00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:15.958
at ease.

105
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:19.875
No great preparation is needed.

106
00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:22.875
Just as ghee is offered

107
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:25.458
in a traditional yajna,

108
00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:28.500
in the same way, you offer your consciousness

109
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:34.125
and awareness into the fire of meditation.

110
00:06:34.125 --> 00:06:36.958
Every moment of chanting

111
00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:40.166
becomes a beautiful offering,

112
00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:44.500
one that purifies your heart and mind.

113
00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.750
Japa is not just a method,

114
00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:52.625
it is a practice that transforms you completely.

115
00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:55.625
Through continuous chanting,

116
00:06:55.625 --> 00:07:00.625
the impurities of your heart, doubts,

117
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:05.333
and confusion slowly begin to diminish.

118
00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:08.583
Your mind becomes calm,

119
00:07:08.583 --> 00:07:11.666
your thoughts become clear,

120
00:07:11.666 --> 00:07:16.166
and your connection with Me deepens.

121
00:07:16.166 --> 00:07:20.625
The beauty of japa lies in its simplicity.

122
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:26.041
Whatever your age or circumstances,

123
00:07:26.041 --> 00:07:30.083
you can chant My sacred names

124
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:34.333
and experience their power.

125
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:37.541
By dedicating your time and energy

126
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:39.916
to this practice,

127
00:07:39.916 --> 00:07:44.875
you are truly performing a yajna of devotion,

128
00:07:44.875 --> 00:07:48.666
which brings peace, joy,

129
00:07:48.666 --> 00:07:52.250
and a sense of divine connection to your life.

130
00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:57.625
Make this your daily spiritual practice.

131
00:07:57.625 --> 00:08:00.708
A simple yet profound way

132
00:08:00.708 --> 00:08:04.041
to keep your heart connected

133
00:08:04.041 --> 00:08:06.791
to purity.

134
00:08:06.791 --> 00:08:10.708
Always chanting My name.

135
00:08:10.708 --> 00:08:14.750
Japa in itself

136
00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.041
is also a great tapa.

137
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:23.333
Among trees,

138
00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:26.166
I am the banyan.

139
00:08:26.166 --> 00:08:29.708
Among elephants, I am Airavata.

140
00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:34.750
Among serpents, I am Vasuki.

141
00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.541
These wonderful qualities of Mine

142
00:08:38.541 --> 00:08:42.000
surely fill you with joyful wonder.

143
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.333
But do

144
00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:47.791
the achievements of the people around you,

145
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:52.541
the praise and recognition they receive,

146
00:08:52.541 --> 00:08:55.416
give you the same joy?

147
00:08:55.416 --> 00:08:59.208
Do you appreciate them,

148
00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:01.125
or do you become envious?

149
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:05.708
Your neighbour's son became a senior officer.

150
00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:10.333
A relative's daughter became a scientist.

151
00:09:10.333 --> 00:09:13.208
What arises in your mind?

152
00:09:13.208 --> 00:09:15.375
Admiration

153
00:09:15.375 --> 00:09:18.208
or envy?

154
00:09:18.208 --> 00:09:20.541
The truth is this –

155
00:09:20.541 --> 00:09:24.958
every talent, every success of theirs

156
00:09:24.958 --> 00:09:26.958
is My blessing.

157
00:09:26.958 --> 00:09:29.750
Through those achievements,

158
00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.625
I Myself am manifesting.

159
00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:36.750
When you understand this,

160
00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:40.500
admiration will take the place of envy.

161
00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.791
You will see Me in their success.

162
00:09:44.791 --> 00:09:48.500
Appreciate your brother's ability.

163
00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.333
Admire your sister's art.

164
00:09:52.333 --> 00:09:58.083
Respect your neighbour's intelligence.

165
00:09:58.083 --> 00:10:00.541
True devotion is

166
00:10:00.541 --> 00:10:03.083
recognising Me

167
00:10:03.083 --> 00:10:06.000
in the virtues of others.

168
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.416
Taking the benefit of those virtues

169
00:10:08.416 --> 00:10:10.750
to improve yourself,

170
00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.375
and being grateful for them.

171
00:10:13.375 --> 00:10:16.750
Then this awareness will teach your family

172
00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:21.500
in place of envy to appreciate.

173
00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.375
Through this, the whole family and society

174
00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:27.833
can grow together.

175
00:10:27.833 --> 00:10:29.958
Let go of envy.

176
00:10:29.958 --> 00:10:32.166
Embrace gratitude.

177
00:10:32.166 --> 00:10:34.541
Remember,

178
00:10:34.541 --> 00:10:37.541
I am in everyone.

179
00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:45.750
Among human beings, I am the king.

180
00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:49.166
The one who upholds dharma,

181
00:10:49.166 --> 00:10:52.375
who gives justice, who protects all.

182
00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:54.291
Imagine,

183
00:10:54.291 --> 00:10:57.666
you are a team leader.

184
00:10:57.666 --> 00:11:00.750
You must make a difficult decision.

185
00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.583
A team member has made a mistake.

186
00:11:03.583 --> 00:11:10.458
Others are pressuring you to punish them.

187
00:11:10.458 --> 00:11:11.875
What will you do?

188
00:11:11.875 --> 00:11:16.583
Before deciding, understand this –

189
00:11:16.583 --> 00:11:19.250
a king or leader

190
00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.583
is not simply someone who sits on a throne.

191
00:11:23.583 --> 00:11:25.625
They are a servant,

192
00:11:25.625 --> 00:11:29.916
one who works for the good of those they lead.

193
00:11:29.916 --> 00:11:32.958
Your position too is the same.

194
00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:36.250
It gives not just authority,

195
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.875
but responsibility too.

196
00:11:37.875 --> 00:11:40.375
Make decisions aligned with dharma.

197
00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:44.208
Never yield to unfair pressure.

198
00:11:44.208 --> 00:11:47.500
Evaluate the team member's mistake

199
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:50.250
with impartiality.

200
00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.833
Protect your colleagues –

201
00:11:52.833 --> 00:11:55.250
do not exploit them.

202
00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.708
If a mistake was made unintentionally,

203
00:11:58.708 --> 00:12:02.666
stand by them. Teach them.

204
00:12:02.666 --> 00:12:06.666
When someone makes a mistake,
give them the opportunity to improve.

205
00:12:06.666 --> 00:12:09.958
When a colleague is under stress,

206
00:12:09.958 --> 00:12:13.250
encourage them and lift their spirits.

207
00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:17.416
True leadership runs the organisation

208
00:12:17.416 --> 00:12:19.416
not through fear, but through love.

209
00:12:19.416 --> 00:12:23.083
Not through intimidation, but through trust.

210
00:12:23.083 --> 00:12:25.500
This is the path of dharma.

211
00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:30.083
This is the definition of true leadership.

212
00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:32.250
Leading is not just

213
00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.625
gaining a high position,

214
00:12:35.625 --> 00:12:39.750
but a golden opportunity for service.

215
00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.875
Always remember this with humility.
